Licensing status of CSBwin
==========================

This repository contains the source of CSBwin, a reverse-engineered port of
the games Dungeon Master and Chaos Strikes Back. It is NOT free software and
is NOT released under the GPL or any other open-source license.

The original games, their artwork, names and game data structures are
copyrighted and trademarked products of Software Heaven, Inc. (FTL Games) and
remain the property of their respective owners. No copyright or trademark
rights to that material are granted by this repository.

CSBwin was created by Paul R. Stevens, who describes its status as follows:

    I translated the game (stole it!!!) from FTL. I cannot claim that it is
    mine to give away. I have always said that as far as I am concerned,
    people can do with it what they please until FTL asks that they do
    otherwise. If FTL complains I will stop distributing it and will attempt
    to notify as many people as possible who might have it. For now, it is
    stolen-ware.

    From: Paul R. Stevens
    To:   Erik Svanberg
    Subject: CSB: COPYING

    This game is really not Freeware. It is Stolenware.

Wayne Holder (producer of DM/CSB, Software Heaven, Inc.) wrote:

    Please be aware that DM and CSB are both copyrighted and trademarked
    products that belong to Software Heaven, Inc (SHI). The FTL swoosh is
    also a trademark of SHI as are the images in the program, the design of
    the game data structures and numerous other aspects of the original
    product. You and your friend have no right to convert this intellectual
    property to GPL because it belongs to SHI.

This repository therefore distributes the source under the same informal
understanding: use it as you please, do not sell it, and be aware that the
underlying game remains the intellectual property of its owners. Game data
files (dungeons, graphics, sounds) are not included and must be obtained
separately.

The original CSBwin sources and binaries are published by Paul R. Stevens at
https://www.dianneandpaul.net/CSBwin/ and described at
http://dmweb.free.fr/community/clones/chaos-strikes-back-for-windows-and-linux-raspbian-macos-x-pocket-pc/

If you are a rights holder and object to this distribution, please open an
issue and it will be removed.
